# v009a: the rotation-averaging ABLATION of v009.
#
# Same image, two environment variables. v009 (rotavg on, 160k px) reaches CV
# rot 2.96; this one turns rotation averaging off and spends the freed runtime
# on resolution instead (255k px), landing at CV ATE 3.80 / rot 5.12 -- nearly
# the same ATE with 1.7x the rotation error.
#
# The pair is deliberate: on DA3 rotation averaging improved CV rot by 19% but
# the improvement transferred badly to the leaderboard (CV 3.98 -> LB 6.04, a
# 1.52x degradation) while its runtime cost pushed W_t to 1.06 and lost more
# score than it gained. Submitting both isolates whether the much larger Pi3X
# gain (-41%) actually survives the transfer, with W_t pinned to 1.0 on both
# sides so the comparison is not confounded by the runtime weight.
FROM climb-pi3x:v009
ENV DA3_ROTAVG=0 PI3_PIXEL_LIMIT=255000
